implementationPlan.description:
4. Bundle pin, Edit tool only, additions only: moe-vscode/tests/blocker-corpus.test.cjs. Append one test, 'C3: ...', after C2 and touch nothing above it. Prototype: /mnt/d/moe-scratch/vsc23-prototype/moe-vscode/tests/blocker-corpus.test.cjs.

- Parse moe-jetbrains/src/main/resources/messages/MoeBundle.properties (UTF-8) with /^moe\.blocker\.([A-Za-z.]+)=(.*?)\r?$/gm.
  - Assert no value holds a backslash, because that would be a properties escape this parser does not decode.
  - Assert the parsed key set equals the keys this test pins, so a new moe.blocker.* key fails until someone maps it. The pinned keys: cause.resourceWait, cause.dependencyWait, cause.externalBlock, the same three under clears., attention.badge, attention.clears, section.title, reason, reason.missing, prerequisites, resourceId, fromStatus, blockedAt.
- The mapping is fixed in the test, never derived from the code under test.
  - On all three surfaces:
    - BLOCK_CAUSE_LABEL[RESOURCE_WAIT | DEPENDENCY_WAIT | EXTERNAL_BLOCK] maps to cause.*;
    - BLOCK_CAUSE_CLEARS[same] maps to clears.*;
    - ATTENTION_LABEL maps to attention.badge, and ATTENTION_CLEARS to attention.clears.
  - On TaskDetailPanel.ts and taskDetail.js only (board.js carries just the card's labels):
    - BLOCKER_SECTION_TITLE to section.title;
    - BLOCKER_REASON_LABEL to reason, and BLOCKER_REASON_MISSING to reason.missing;
    - BLOCKER_PREREQUISITES_LABEL to prerequisites;
    - BLOCKER_RESOURCE_LABEL to resourceId;
    - BLOCKER_FROM_STATUS_LABEL to fromStatus;
    - BLOCKER_BLOCKED_AT_LABEL to blockedAt.
- Read the panel's copy from panelModule's exports. Read the board.js and taskDetail.js copies inside the contexts this file already loads, with vm.runInContext.
  - board.js declares its copies with top-level const, which never becomes a context property.
  - JSON-stringify inside the context to leave the vm realm.
- Each surface's two maps must name exactly the three causes.
- Collect every value mismatch as '<surface> moe.blocker.<key>: expected <bundle value>, got <value>' and assert the list empty once, at the end. Use the existing SURFACES names TaskDetailPanel.ts, board.js and taskDetail.js, because checkref 3 greps '<surface> moe.blocker.clears'.

All three copies match today, so C3 passes at once; checkref 3 proves it catches a drift in each copy.

Size: at most 40 added lines. The prototype adds 37.
